{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Design decision (session with operator, 2026-07-29): resolve this as part of jira-reb-1582, not independently.\n\nRoot cause confirmed by reading the resolver. resolve_hierarchy_link (src/rebar/graph/_hierarchy.py:98) defines \"comparable level\" by TICKET TYPE TIER (_TYPE_TIER: epic=2, story=1, task/bug=0) and promotes the lower-tier endpoint up its parent chain to the first ancestor at the higher tier. In the repro, T1 (task, tier 0) depends_on S (story, tier 1) with both as direct children of epic E: the resolver looks for a tier-1 (story) ancestor of T1, walks the chain [T1, E], finds none (E is tier 2), and hits the chain-root fallback at _hierarchy.py:93 -- returning E. Hence E depends_on its own child S.\n\nUnder jira-reb-1582s structural rule (comparability = sharing a parent, not sharing a type) this is unreachable: T1 and S are siblings, so the link records exactly as requested with no promotion. So 1803 is a symptom of the type-tier policy, and its repro becomes a regression test on the 1582 change rather than a separate fix.\n\nSecond defect found while tracing, to be fixed in the same change: add_dependency (src/rebar/graph/_links.py:180) raises on is_redundant, but is_redundant is computed by the resolver from the ORIGINAL source/target pair, before promotion. T1->S is not redundant; the promoted E->S is, and nothing re-checks it. The guard must be applied to the RESOLVED pair, and generalized from \"direct parent-child\" to \"any ancestor/descendant\" -- a hard invariant that a ticket never blocks its own subtree regardless of how the edge was produced (including via later re-parenting).\n\nStatus: no code claimed or written yet."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785370704805958001,"uuid":"d7cd8d44-dd16-406d-943d-e86dc3394f09"}